APS-008 — Policy Lifecycle

Document ID: APS-008
Title: Policy Lifecycle
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Policy Lifecycle Model (CPLM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Policy Lifecycle Model establishes the governed progression of Canonical Policy Objects from initial authoring through review, approval, publication, activation, supersession, retirement, and archival while preserving traceability, governance, and engineering integrity.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Policy lifecycle architecture
Lifecycle states
State transitions
Rollout model
Effective periods
Supersession
Rollback
Lifecycle governance

This specification applies to every Canonical Policy Object.

3. Canonical Definition

A Policy Lifecycle is the governed sequence of operational states through which a Canonical Policy Object progresses from creation until retirement while preserving identity, governance, and historical continuity.

The lifecycle governs the operational availability of a policy.

It does not govern policy evaluation.

4. Objectives

The Policy Lifecycle SHALL:

Standardize policy evolution.
Enable controlled rollout.
Preserve historical versions.
Support governance.
Enable safe retirement.
Support rollback.
Enable auditability.
Preserve policy continuity.
5. Lifecycle Principles

Every Canonical Policy Object SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Governed Progression

Lifecycle transitions SHALL occur only through authorized governance processes.

Immutable Releases

Published policy versions SHALL NOT be modified.

Version Continuity

Every lifecycle transition SHALL preserve policy lineage.

Controlled Activation

Policies SHALL become operational only after successful approval.

Historical Preservation

Retired policies SHALL remain permanently traceable.

Reversible Deployment

Policy activation SHOULD support rollback where operationally feasible.

6. Canonical Lifecycle States

Atlas defines the following canonical lifecycle states.

State	Description
Draft	Policy under development
Under Review	Technical and governance review
Approved	Governance approval completed
Published	Officially released
Scheduled	Awaiting effective date
Active	Governing operational behavior
Suspended	Temporarily inactive
Superseded	Replaced by a newer policy
Deprecated	Supported but scheduled for removal
Retired	No longer applicable
Archived	Preserved for historical reference

Future policy profiles MAY extend these states while preserving canonical semantics.

