8. Effective Period

Every policy SHALL define:

Effective From
Effective Until (optional)
Activation conditions
Expiration conditions

A published policy SHALL NOT become active before its effective period.

9. Rollout Model

Atlas supports the following rollout strategies.

Strategy	Description
Immediate	Activated immediately after publication
Scheduled	Activated at a specified time
Phased	Activated incrementally
Conditional	Activated when defined conditions are met
Manual	Activated through explicit authorization

The selected strategy SHALL be explicitly declared.

10. Supersession

A superseded policy SHALL:

Reference the replacing policy.
Preserve historical versions.
Preserve evaluation history.
Preserve audit records.
Remain resolvable.

Supersession SHALL NOT invalidate historical policy decisions.

11. Rollback

Rollback SHALL support:

Previous approved version
Rollback justification
Approval authority
Rollback timestamp
Impact assessment

Rollback SHALL create a new lifecycle event rather than modifying historical records.

12. Lifecycle Events

Policy lifecycle transitions MAY generate Canonical Events.

Examples include:

Policy Submitted
Policy Approved
Policy Published
Policy Activated
Policy Suspended
Policy Superseded
Policy Retired

Events SHALL conform to ADS-006 — Canonical Event (CEV).

13. Lifecycle Governance

Every policy lifecycle SHALL define:

Author
Reviewer
Approver
Release authority
Retirement authority
Governance domain
Applicable policies

Lifecycle governance SHALL remain independently auditable.

14. Quality Gates

Lifecycle transitions MAY require mandatory quality gates.

Examples include:

Transition	Quality Gate
Draft → Under Review	Structural validation
Under Review → Approved	Governance review
Approved → Published	Compliance verification
Published → Active	Deployment authorization
Active → Retired	Impact assessment

Quality gates SHALL be explicitly defined.

15. Policy Availability

Atlas distinguishes between lifecycle state and operational availability.

Examples:

Lifecycle State	Operational Availability
Draft	Not Available
Published	Available for Deployment
Scheduled	Pending Activation
Active	Governing Runtime
Suspended	Temporarily Disabled
Retired	Historical Only

Operational availability SHALL remain independently observable.

16. Conformance

A Policy Lifecycle implementation conforms if it:

Implements canonical lifecycle states.
Supports governed transitions.
Preserves policy history.
Supports rollout strategies.
Supports supersession.
Supports rollback.
Maintains lifecycle traceability.
17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Progressive rollout by governance domain.
Automatic rollback policies.
AI-assisted impact prediction.
Multi-jurisdiction policy activation.
Canary deployments for policy changes.
Continuous policy deployment pipelines.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical lifecycle semantics.

